From cf3bba5c26df3ad912c29b71dd0bf5d3f6d6b652 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ake Rehnman <ake.rehnman@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 18:11:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ui: decouple GL presentation from renderer blocking

GTK and SPICE currently hold the global virtio-gpu renderer block until
frontend presentation completes. This couples control and Venus command
progress to the display cadence and native display fences.

Copy each completed guest scanout into bounded frontend-owned mailbox
storage instead. Hold the renderer block only while the asynchronous copy
consumes the guest resource, then let GTK and SPICE present the private
copy at their own cadence.

Coalesce pending frames and retain active SPICE slots until GL_DRAW_DONE
so neither resource lifetime nor producer ordering is weakened.

Signed-off-by: Ake Rehnman <ake.rehnman@gmail.com>
